# Shell scripts are checked out with LF everywhere.  release-nunchaku.yml runs
# .github/scripts/*.sh from a `bash -l {0}` step on windows-latest (Git-Bash),
# and a CRLF `set -euo pipefail\r` fails that shell before it does anything.
# Today the runner leaves core.autocrlf off, so the leg is green -- but that is
# a runner-image default, not a guarantee.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The Windows launcher must ship BYTE FOR BYTE: scripts/pack.sh copies it into
# the package and `cmp`s the copy, and it was verified as-is on a real Windows
# VM.  It is LF in the index (measured: `git show :windows/isabelle.bat | od -c`
# starts `@ e c h o   o f f \n`, and no commit that ever touched it had CRLF),
# so this rule exists to stop git normalising it in EITHER direction, not to
# preserve CRLF.  Kept last because git's last matching rule wins, so a future
# `*` rule above cannot reach it.
#
# The files that genuinely must be CRLF are the .bat link hooks the recipe
# GENERATES at build time; nothing here touches those, and the recipe asserts
# their line endings itself.
*.bat -text
